   "etymology": "From i (masculine definite article) + në (from ne, first person plural pronoun).\nCompare jonë, from jo (original form of the feminine definite article, weakened to -a) + në.\nOld accusative form tënë from të+në. Compare the accusative pronoun atë.\nOld dative-genitive masculine tinë from ti (today would've yielded ty, compare the possessive adjective for relatives tyt as in tyt vëllai and the dative pronoun atij.\nOld ablative masculine sinë from si (surviving in the antiquated pronoun asi) +në.",
